{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122443","id":4286607667,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7_gHEz","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122443","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122443.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122443.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122443","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122443/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122443/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122443/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/bce929dbf2a1aede0e261f621ff90d35ca4e70fd","number":122443,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"🤖 Use `GDSOFTCLASS` for internal `NativeMenu` and 2D navigation implementations","user":{"login":"kevinlincg","id":3426764,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MjY3NjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3426764?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinlincg","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinlincg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinlincg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinlincg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinlincg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinlincg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinlincg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinlincg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinlincg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinlincg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinlincg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes _maintainer edit: not_ #120370\r\n\r\n`NativeMenuMacOS`, `NativeMenuWindows` and `GodotNavigationServer2D` are internal\r\nimplementations. They are never registered in `ClassDB` via `ClassDB::register_class()`\r\nand define no `_bind_methods()`. However, `GDCLASS` adds them to `ClassDB` anyway through\r\n`initialize_class()`, so `ClassDB.get_class_list()` lists them even though scripts cannot\r\nreference them:\r\n\r\n    SCRIPT ERROR: Parse Error: Identifier \"GodotNavigationServer2D\" not declared in the current scope.\r\n\r\n`GDSOFTCLASS` exists for exactly this case — its doc comment states it is for \"`Object`\r\nsubclasses that are not registered in `ClassDB`\". This is the same fix already applied to\r\nthe internal `IP` implementations in ce098a9264.\r\n\r\nNote that `GodotNavigationServer3D` already does not use `GDCLASS`, so the 2D counterpart\r\nwas inconsistent with it.\r\n\r\nNeither class has a `doc/classes/*.xml` entry, which is further indication that they were\r\nnot intended to be exposed.\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\nBuilt on macOS (x86_64, OpenGL3/Compatibility) and inspected `ClassDB.get_class_list()`\r\nfrom a script:\r\n\r\n| Class | before | after |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `GodotNavigationServer2D` | listed | not listed |\r\n| `NativeMenuMacOS` | listed | not listed |\r\n\r\n`NativeMenuMacOS` is only added to `ClassDB` once `DisplayServerMacOS` instantiates it, so\r\nthis requires a non-headless run to observe. `NativeMenuWindows` receives the identical\r\nchange but was not verified locally (no Windows machine available); it is covered by CI.\r\n\r\nChecked for functional regressions:\r\n\r\n- `NativeMenu.has_feature(FEATURE_GLOBAL_MENU)` still returns `true` and\r\n  `get_system_menu(MAIN_MENU_ID)` still returns a valid RID, confirming the platform\r\n  implementation is still in use.\r\n- `NavigationServer2D` map and agent creation/destruction still work.\r\n- Full unit test suite passes: 1419 test cases, 421648 assertions, 0 failed.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n> [!NOTE]\r\n> **AI disclosure**: This contribution was authored with the assistance of an autonomous AI\r\n> coding agent (Claude), acting on my behalf. The agent identified the root cause, made the\r\n> change, and ran the builds and verification described above. I reviewed the result before\r\n> submitting.\r\n","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":6051509301,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABaLK0NQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/spam","name":"spam","description":"","color":"E94A26","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-08-15T14:48:47Z","updated_at":"2026-08-15T15:57:15Z","closed_at":"2026-08-15T15:55:22Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"ba903df97911ed3a0d72f3a3351d73534f7d904a","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"kevinlincg:fix-internal-classes-leaking-into-classdb","ref":"fix-internal-classes-leaking-into-classdb","repo":{"id":1335163204,"node_id":"R_kgDOT5T5RA","name":"godot","full_name":"kevinlincg/godot","owner":{"login":"kevinlincg","id":3426764,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MjY3NjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3426764?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinlincg","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinlincg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinlincg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinlincg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinlincg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinlincg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinlincg/subscriptions","organization